# Practical 3 — File Upload Implementation (Frontend: React/Next.js)

## Overview

This project implements a **client-side file upload interface** using React (via Next.js). It features a drag-and-drop upload zone, file type and size validation, real-time upload progress tracking, and PDF preview support — all connected to an Express backend (see the companion backend README).

---

## Features

- **Drag and drop interface** using `react-dropzone`
- **File type validation** — accepts JPEG, PNG, and PDF only
- **File size validation** — rejects files larger than 5MB
- **Upload progress bar** — real-time progress via Axios's `onUploadProgress`
- **Image preview** — shows image thumbnail before upload
- **PDF indicator** — shows filename and icon for PDF files
- **Success/error feedback** — displays upload result with file details
- **Form management** with `react-hook-form`

---

## Tech Stack

| Package | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `next.js` | React framework and development environment |
| `react-hook-form` | Form state management and validation |
| `axios` | HTTP client with upload progress support |
| `react-dropzone` | Drag-and-drop file input component |
| `formidable` | (Used in API route) Server-side multipart form parsing |

